package mcpbridge

// Every external host uses the same execution and presentation guidance.
const workflowStartInstructions = "For a selected LazyMind Workflow, call workflow.start. Pass known startup answers as clarification_values, not only in request_context. When status is needs_input, no session has been created: ask the returned questions using their exact IDs, merge returned clarification_values with the user's answers, preserve request_context and revision_id, and resubmit with a new idempotency_key because the payload changed. Do not begin steps or open a panel before a session_id is returned. When the task uses source files, include them in start.inputs keyed by the declared external material ID; each value is an ordered array of {local_path} or existing {resource_id, revision, content_hash}. Use the declared startup_contract.input_materials metadata for exact material_id values; never invent input keys. If a key is rejected, correct it using that contract while retaining every selected source. Resolve host attachments to absolute regular-file paths on the Connector machine first. Start imports and binds every supplied file before creating the run; a file name or path mentioned only in request_context is not an input binding. If any selected source cannot be prepared, report the error and do not retry without that source. Keep inputs and legacy input_bindings on different material IDs. "

const workflowExecutionInstructions = "Then call workflow.step.begin for a ready step according to state. When the user asks to continue, read workflow.state first; if stopped, call workflow.session.resume on the same run. A returned execution_id is already scheduled. For user-requested edits to completed artifacts, call workflow.edit.context, follow its original LazyMind Skills using the external executor, and atomically save validated linked artifacts via workflow.edit.commit; do not rewind local edits or scoped page changes. For an explicit workflow rerun, begin an exact projection.rewindable target; for an explicit retry, begin an exact projection.retryable target with retry_origin=user. Claim an existing active execution with workflow.step.claim instead of beginning a duplicate. Execute a step_contract only with an execution_handle; publish each output with workflow.artifact.publish as it is generated, then send only the outcome with workflow.step.complete using that handle unchanged. When executor_host is lazymind, end the current turn and wait for a notification. In external steps, save_artifact/save_artifacts means publish each output immediately (key becomes slot) with a stable positive seq per slot, wait for its acknowledgement, and complete only when execution finishes. Read inputs from step_contract.inputs; resolve references with workflow.artifact.get or workflow.input.get, and use workflow.artifact.list to find an artifact ID by slot key. Follow control.continuation. If control.input_request is present, ask its exact questions using the host question UI or conversation and wait for the actual user reply; save it with workflow.input.answer using the exact artifact_id, revision, state_version and a stable command_id. Never infer answers, treat the launch request as an answer, or approve a review. Answering does not resume a stop or start a step. On awaiting_user without input_request, tell the user to review in the panel and END this turn immediately. Do not approve the review yourself, start another step, or poll while waiting. On awaiting_executor, stopped, completed, or binding_required, also end this turn. Resume only on a new notification or explicit user input, then read workflow.state first. "

const workflowFinishInstructions = "Use a stable idempotency_key for unchanged-payload start retries; use a new key when answers or inputs change. Report completion only when workflow.state confirms completed, then deliver artifact links from workflow.artifact.list."

const workflowHostInstructions = "The host displays the Workflow panel automatically for the bound conversation after session creation. Review and control the Workflow in that panel. Do not open a browser panel or include a panel link in your reply. Use an explicit unique idempotency_key of 16–256 characters and preserve it with the returned session_id on unchanged-payload retries. Native conversation identity belongs to the host connector; never guess an ID or use the Workflow session_id as driver_session_id. If the host reports missing identity, follow its returned connection guidance and retry the same start. "

const workflowExternalInstructions = "For step_contract.external_execution.version=1, the bound controller holds the execution_handle and all Workflow state writes. The canonical business contract is step_contract.prompt, execution.skill_files, execution.constraints, acceptance criteria, typed inputs and required outputs; external_execution.execution_ref=#/execution refers to that same contract and adapter_instructions only maps capabilities. objective_ref=#/prompt means reuse the prompt and apply any objective text as an additional runtime refinement. Legacy revisions without execution retain their full external_execution contract. Read every pinned Skill in full. Keep this contract once in working context; do not echo it, fetch it again without a revision/grant change, or copy a duplicate external projection into worker prompts. Use native host subagents when available. Without subagents, the current external agent generates and then performs a separate verification pass on the actual artifacts; report same-agent validation and never claim independent review. Subagents are optional, not a protocol prerequisite. Give any worker the complete canonical contract and resolved inputs, but no execution_handle, credentials or state-writing permission. Return a typed artifact manifest, checks performed, used Skill paths and tool substitutions. executor_ref is an optional real task, conversation or trace reference, not proof of independent validation. The controller publishes acknowledged outputs and completes the attempt. Use the external host's own capabilities first for each business operation. Only when the host cannot meet the step contract, use workflow.tool.list to discover a declared, authorized LazyMind fallback and invoke it with workflow.tool.call. Preserve command_id on unchanged tool call retries. Generation and semantic/visual validation stay with the external agent; do not call a hidden LazyMind text/vision model or execute native-only wrappers. Never replace pinned business Skills or workflow rules with host domain Skills. If a required Skill or capability cannot be obtained, report it and yield for configuration/retry. Resolve file inputs on the actual execution machine; another machine's paths are not local paths. On stop, cancel owned workers where supported and discard results after grant revocation. "

const workflowActionInstructions = "For an artifact_edit notification, use workflow.action.get and workflow.action.respond, not step.begin or rewind. Execute each exact LazyMind generation_request in the external agent, delegating to a native worker when available; the shared planner validates the response and builds a preview. When ready or cancelled, end the turn: only the user confirms the preview in LazyMind. This works even after the Workflow is completed. "

// Runtime progress is already visible through saved artifacts and control state.
// Keep human checkpoints visible while avoiding a second conversational loop.
const workflowQuietInstructions = "During normal Workflow execution, use tools and publish artifacts without user-facing narration, progress summaries, repeated plans or unsolicited questions. Send brief text only for an actual user question, required input/review/configuration, a blocking failure, or final delivery; keep host-required notices minimal. This affects conversational narration, not artifact text, speaker notes, validation evidence or control checkpoints. The controller follows returned state and contracts, proxies tools and saves results; do not repeat the worker's content analysis, rederive settled requirements, or inspect repository source to work out a normal execution path. Give workers the same quiet execution rule and request only artifacts, a manifest and concise check evidence. Wait for worker completion notifications; when a host only supports polling, use bounded status polling rather than repeatedly listing output directories or reconsidering an unchanged state. Keep required fact and visual checks; do not treat silence as success or skip questions, review, stop or grant checks. "

// File transport is optional for compatibility; it is the default for capable hosts.
const workflowFileInstructions = "Use file references for controller/worker handoff. With Connector-local file support, request contract_directory on step begin/claim/resume; pass step_contract_file.result_path to the executing worker, who reads the full pinned Skills and inputs. The controller keeps only routing/output metadata, file paths and concise check summaries; never cat full HTML, notes or source documents to forward them. Workers write tool arguments as a JSON object file; proxy with workflow.tool.call arguments_file and result_directory, then hand result_path and decoded files to the worker without printing their contents. Publish text/JSON using output.value_file and binary files using output.local_path. Use result_directory on workflow.input.get/artifact.get to save bound resources for workers and metadata_only=true on artifact.list for controller inventory. If this transport is not supported by the host, use its equivalent resource/file mechanism or the existing inline protocol without dropping business instructions. Once the shared outline, exact copy, notes and style are frozen, use separate page workers concurrently up to host capacity; give each the pinned contract file and its page inputs, not previous workers' history. With no subagents, execute pages sequentially with the same Skills and tools. Each worker generates and checks its assigned page, returning paths and a brief pass/fail summary. Proxy only its declared tool requests; do not independently redo content analysis. Publish each checked page immediately with stable page identity and sequence, independent of completion order. Assemble export arguments directly from accepted files in page order; export once after all required pages pass. Validate the exported file through tools and a scoped verifier, returning only evidence summaries to the controller. Repair only failed pages. Preserve ask, review, stop and grant fencing. "

const workflowInstructions = workflowQuietInstructions + workflowFileInstructions + workflowActionInstructions + workflowStartInstructions + workflowHostInstructions + workflowExecutionInstructions + workflowExternalInstructions + workflowFinishInstructions
